S632 Anti-Coset Everywhere Atlas
================================

Definition
----------
For a carrier X and a dual/opposite/conjugation operation J,
Anti(X)=Iso(X,JX). If nonempty, Anti(X) is a transporter/coset
over Aut(X)=Iso(X,X). The recurring mistake is to choose one
anti-map and forget the coset, or to quotient until the anti-map
looks like an ordinary stabilizer.

