Full centered hex shells (n=1,7,19) keep the full D6 anti-coset.
Partial shell prefixes usually retain only a small or empty anti-coset,
which is the finite carrier version of the 'Eisenstein pattern ends'
warning beyond the first complete shell.

4. Tournament Analysis over anti-coset lenses
---------------------------------------------
Vertices are carrier lenses. Pairwise observable: which lens keeps
the transporter, side-channel, and quotient-loss data most explicitly.
Switches/gauges: SC torsor theorem, LRC shell action, Eisenstein D6
conjugation. Tie HP: majority tournament over the three gauges.
score_hist={0: 1, 1: 1, 2: 1, 3: 1, 4: 1, 5: 1} directed_3cycles=0 H=1
